{"id": "unknown-2026-10-26-001", "date": "2026-10-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 44, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Update: Qingyue's IPO sponsor, auditor and actual controller set up a 370 million RMB fund to compensate investors", "content": "<p>On October 23, 2026, <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/qingyue\">Qingyue Technology</a>'s IPO sponsor GF Securities announced that it has set up a 370 million RMB (around $55.5 million USD) special fund to compensate investors who lost money in the company's shares. The fund was established jointly by GF Securities, Qingyue's auditor BDO China Shu Lun Pan Certified Public Accountants and Gao Yudi, Qingyue's actual controller, and the money has already been fully transferred into a supervised ", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/update-qingyues-ipo-sponsor-auditor-and-actual-controller-set-370-million-rmb", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-26-002", "date": "2026-10-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 44, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Counterpoint: laptop mini-LED shipments to drop 75% within two years, as OLED takes over the premium laptop market", "content": "<p>According to new estimates from Counterpoint Research (DSCS), global shipments of mini-LED panels for laptops will decrease by 38% in 2026, and by a further 60% in 2027 - so 2027 shipments will reach only about 25% of their 2025 level. Laptop OLED panel shipments, on the other hand, are projected to grow by 50% in 2026 and by another 24% in 2027, while the overall laptop display market is expected to shrink by 3% this year.</p><p><img class=\"align-center\" src=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sites/", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/counterpoint-laptop-mini-led-shipments-drop-75-within-two-years-oled-takes-over", "type": "rss"}]}
