{"id": "unknown-2026-10-26-011", "date": "2026-10-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 44, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration", "automotive_display"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Dowoo Insys develops ultra-thin glass for rollable automotive OLED displays, aims for commercialization in 2027-2028", "content": "<p>Korea-based <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/dowoo-insys\">Dowoo Insys</a>, which produces ultra-thin glass (UTG) cover windows for foldable OLEDs, is reportedly developing UTG for rollable automotive OLED displays, in cooperation with a major Korean automotive electronics company. The glass is aimed at rollable center information displays (CIDs) and entertainment screens, and commercialization could begin as early as the second half of 2027.</p><a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sites/defau", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/dowoo-insys-develops-ultra-thin-glass-rollable-automotive-oled-displays-aims", "type": "rss"}]}
